\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Moments at fixed and separated times}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The moment limits in \ref{fdip-00I6} control smooth averages
over spacetime. The [reflected pairing](fdip-007M) also needs a
positive-time domain, while a Hamiltonian interpretation involves
fields at fixed times. Which additional estimates connect these
uses of time? The hypotheses are stated in
\citet{Axioms A-C, pp. 273-275}{frohlich1974verification}.}
